---
import NoteFigure from './NoteFigure.astro';

const curve = (mean: number) => Array.from({ length: 131 }, (_, i) => {
  const x = 40 + i * 2;
  const y = 275 - 80 * Math.exp(-0.5 * ((x - mean) / 27) ** 2);
  return `${i ? 'L' : 'M'} ${x.toFixed(1)} ${y.toFixed(2)}`;
}).join(' ');
---

<NoteFigure
  label="Training bound"
  title="Separate the endpoints, then match interior posterior means"
  caption="Reconstructed from the three-term bound on page 42 and the two-Gaussian mean-matching sketch on page 43. The cards show the roles of the terms, with no loss magnitudes implied. The Gaussian curves are schematic equal-variance distributions at one interior step, illustrating the choice σₜ² = β̃ₜ; their axes have no empirical units. Endpoint qualifications and the panel layout are editorial additions."
>
  <div class="elbo-panels">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 340 450" role="img" aria-labelledby="ddpm-elbo-terms-title ddpm-elbo-terms-desc">
      <title id="ddpm-elbo-terms-title">The negative ELBO separates terminal prior matching, interior denoising and reconstruction</title>
      <desc id="ddpm-elbo-terms-desc">Negative log likelihood is upper bounded by L, the negative ELBO. L consists of terminal KL comparing q x T given x zero with the prior, a sum of interior KL terms for timesteps two through T comparing the clean-conditioned posterior with the learned transition, and a reconstruction negative log likelihood at timestep one. The diagram assigns no numerical heights or values to these terms.</desc>
      <defs>
        <marker id="ddpm-elbo-terms-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto"><path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="arrowhead" /></marker>
      </defs>
      <text x="170" y="25" text-anchor="middle" class="panel-title">The complete negative ELBO</text>
      <text x="170" y="61" text-anchor="middle" class="formula">−log p<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">θ</tspan>(x₀) ≤ L(x₀)</text>
      <path d="M 170 72 V 93" class="arrow" marker-end="url(#ddpm-elbo-terms-arrow)" />
      <rect x="23" y="100" width="294" height="83" rx="4" class="node" />
      <text x="39" y="126" class="term-title">Terminal KL · t = T</text>
      <text x="39" y="152">q(x<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">T</tspan> | x₀) versus p(x<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">T</tspan>)</text>
      <text x="39" y="174" class="muted">Constant in θ for a fixed schedule and prior.</text>
      <text x="170" y="207" text-anchor="middle" class="symbol muted">+</text>
      <rect x="23" y="218" width="294" height="93" rx="4" class="interior" />
      <text x="39" y="244" class="term-title accent">Interior KL sum · t = 2, …, T</text>
      <text x="39" y="270">q(x<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">t−1</tspan> | x<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">t</tspan>, x₀) versus p<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">θ</tspan>(x<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">t−1</tspan> | x<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">t</tspan>)</text>
      <text x="39" y="299" class="muted">Average over noisy x<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">t</tspan> drawn from q.</text>
      <text x="170" y="335" text-anchor="middle" class="symbol muted">+</text>
      <rect x="23" y="346" width="294" height="83" rx="4" class="node" />
      <text x="39" y="372" class="term-title">Reconstruction · t = 1</text>
      <text x="39" y="398">−E<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">q</tspan> log p<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">θ</tspan>(x₀ | x₁)</text>
      <text x="39" y="420" class="muted">A decoder likelihood, not an interior KL.</text>
    </svg>

    <svg viewBox="0 0 340 450" role="img" aria-labelledby="ddpm-elbo-means-title ddpm-elbo-means-desc">
      <title id="ddpm-elbo-means-title">With a fixed equal variance, an interior Gaussian KL is a squared error between means</title>
      <desc id="ddpm-elbo-means-desc">At a timestep greater than or equal to two, the exact training posterior has mean tilde mu t and the model has mean mu theta. Two schematic bell curves have the same positive variance. A horizontal arrow links the means. Choosing model variance sigma t squared equal to target variance tilde beta t makes the KL equal to squared mean distance divided by two sigma t squared. The clean-conditioned target is available in training.</desc>
      <defs>
        <marker id="ddpm-elbo-means-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto"><path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="accent-head" /></marker>
      </defs>
      <text x="170" y="25" text-anchor="middle" class="panel-title">Fixed variance: match means</text>
      <text x="170" y="61" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Interior step only: t ≥ 2</text>
      <text x="170" y="99" text-anchor="middle" class="formula">target q: N(μ̃<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">t</tspan>, β̃<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">t</tspan>I)</text>
      <text x="170" y="129" text-anchor="middle" class="formula accent">model p<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">θ</tspan>: N(μ<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">θ</tspan>, σ<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">t</tspan>²I)</text>
      <text x="170" y="159" text-anchor="middle">Here choose σ<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">t</tspan>² = β̃<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">t</tspan> &gt; 0.</text>
      <path d="M 32 276 H 307" class="axis" />
      <path d={curve(119)} class="target-curve" />
      <path d={curve(221)} class="model-curve" />
      <path d="M 119 197 V 276 M 221 197 V 276" class="guide" />
      <text x="119" y="301" text-anchor="middle" class="formula">μ̃<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">t</tspan></text>
      <text x="221" y="301" text-anchor="middle" class="formula accent">μ<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">θ</tspan></text>
      <path d="M 211 318 H 129" class="mean-arrow" marker-end="url(#ddpm-elbo-means-arrow)" />
      <text x="170" y="342" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">learn to bring the means together</text>
      <rect x="29" y="363" width="282" height="47" rx="4" class="interior" />
      <text x="170" y="394" text-anchor="middle" class="formula">KL = ∥μ̃<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">t</tspan> − μ<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">θ</tspan>∥² / (2σ<tspan baseline-shift="sub" class="subscript">t</tspan>²)</text>
      <text x="170" y="438" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Positive fixed unequal variances add a constant.</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
</NoteFigure>

<style>
  .elbo-panels { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; }
  svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; max-width: 400px; margin-inline: auto; }
  text { fill: var(--ink); font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 15px; }
  .panel-title { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; }
  .term-title { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; }
  .symbol { font-size: 24px; }
  .formula { font-size: 17px; }
  .subscript { font-size: 11px; }
  .muted { fill: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }
  .accent { fill: var(--accent); }
  .node { fill: var(--paper); stroke: var(--line); stroke-width: 1.3; }
  .interior { fill: var(--paper); stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1.3; }
  .arrow, .arrowhead { fill: none; stroke: var(--ink); stroke-width: 1.5; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }
  .axis { fill: none; stroke: var(--line); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .target-curve { fill: none; stroke: var(--ink); stroke-width: 1.8; }
  .model-curve { fill: none; stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1.8; }
  .guide { fill: none; stroke: var(--line); stroke-width: 1; stroke-dasharray: 3 4; }
  .mean-arrow, .accent-head { fill: none; stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1.5; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }
  @container (max-width: 580px) { .elbo-panels { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2rem; } }
</style>
